  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Two key kinds — do not conflate",
      "items": [
        "Content keys (MLS/HPKE/Ed25519) protect messages and live only on the two end devices; middle services hold none (second row).",
        "The login bridge key PEERS_OAUTH_BRIDGE_SECRET does not protect content: it is a shared HMAC held by both Station and the OAuth Broker to verify login callbacks."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "How the bridge key reaches Station (make station)",
      "items": [
        "The authoritative value is configured at the OAuth Broker (Vercel); the same value is written to the env repo per-role git-crypt runtime.env.",
        "At make station, deploy ships it over SSH/TLS with the namespaced runtime.env to the host (0600), and compose injects it into the Station container.",
        "The red vertical link between Broker and Station/Relay host secrets means the same bridge secret (HMAC); a missing value fails closed at deploy/startup.",
        "Bottom row: SQLCipher+OS keychain, host-generated AUTH/DB secrets, and git-crypt-deployed secrets; product code ships no deployment-secret crypto."
      ]
    }
  ]
